%I A401231 #28 Oct 23 2026 10:04:03
%S A401231 150,294,1694,2535,7942,9295,17986,31958,34385,42959,44890,49011,
%T A401231 61798,72897,79781,111853,178215,181138,254035,287086,310403,323727,
%U A401231 323733,401233,414239,535279,553479,710677,721463,819478,892463,924161,1268861,1412185,1474742,1791167,2273327,2350079,2801545,2930474,2944597
%N A401231 Numbers of the form p^2*q*r where p, q, r are primes with p > q > r, and p divides A276085(p^2*q*r), where A276085 is fully additive with a(p) = p#/p.
%C A401231 The condition is a necessary (but not sufficient) condition for a term of A398863 being included in A373487. Such terms seem to be quite rare: 278638999, 367794667, 1043816933, etc., see A401371. The terms k for which A276085(k) < A003415(k) seem to be limited to the three initial terms: 150, 294, 1694.
%C A401231 A subsequence of these terms is obtained by multiplying A401057(n)^2 with any two such (distinct) lesser primes q satisfying the condition of A401057. E.g. 19^2 * 11 * 2 = 7942, the fifth term of this sequence. Similarly for terms 49499^2 * 43517 * 7853 = 837312155380890001, 49499^2 * 44279 * 7853 = 851973824668759987, and 49499^2 * 44279 * 43517 = 4721169607552582243.
%H A401231 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A401231/b401231.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1020</a>
%H A401231 <a href="/index/Pri#primorial_numbers">Index entries for sequences related to primorial numbers</a>.
%o A401231 (PARI)
%o A401231 A276085_mod_m(n,m) = if(1==n,0,my(f = factor(n),lp=f[#f~,1],pr=1,s=0,k=1); forprime(p=2,lp,if(f[k,1]==p, s += f[k,2]*pr; s %= m; k++); pr *= p; pr %= m); (s));
%o A401231 is_A401231(k) = { my(f=factor(k)); (3==#f~ && f[1,2]==1 && f[2,2]==1 && f[3,2]==2 && !A276085_mod_m(k,f[3,1])); };
%Y A401231 Cf. A276085, A373487, A401057, A401072 [the count of terms of this sequence whose gpf = prime(n)].
%Y A401231 Intersection of A398863 and A401232. Subsequence of A401233.
%Y A401231 Cf. A401371 (subsequence).
%Y A401231 Cf. also A401229.
%K A401231 nonn,new
%O A401231 1,1
%A A401231 _Antti Karttunen_, Oct 21 2026
